1
00:00:02,535 --> 00:00:04,537
<i>This is the procedure Daimon used.</i>

2
00:00:05,538 --> 00:00:07,474
<i>April 2005.</i>

3
00:00:07,907 --> 00:00:09,909
<i>The gastrointestinal surgery team</i>

4
00:00:09,976 --> 00:00:12,645
<i>at the Cubanancan Medical</i>
<i>University Hospital in Cuba,</i>

5
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:18,718
<i>succeeded in a vascular graft surgery</i>
<i>of the superior mesenteric artery</i>

6
00:00:19,352 --> 00:00:24,791
<i>and brought the hope</i>
<i>of a complete cure to the patient.</i>

7
00:00:25,458 --> 00:00:28,862
<i>However, the patient died</i>
<i>one month after the surgery.</i>

8
00:00:30,597 --> 00:00:33,099
<i>The cause of death</i>
<i>has not been made clear.</i>

9
00:00:33,967 --> 00:00:38,405
<i>Seeking the cause, the family filed</i>
<i>a lawsuit against the hospital.</i>

10
00:00:38,671 --> 00:00:41,775
<i>However, to this day,</i>
<i>the hospital has not released</i>

11
00:00:41,841 --> 00:00:46,179
<i>the identity of the primary surgeon,</i>
<i>Doctor X.</i>

12
00:00:54,921 --> 00:00:58,758
Do you know someone called Doctor X?

13
00:01:01,661 --> 00:01:05,565
The one who's been pulling off
a number of miraculous surgeries,

14
00:01:06,366 --> 00:01:08,034
Doctor X.

15
00:01:10,136 --> 00:01:11,905
Doctor X?

16
00:01:13,306 --> 00:01:16,576
I hear this person has quite a large debt,

17
00:01:17,043 --> 00:01:20,380
and performed
some shady surgeries for money.

18
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:23,416
You know this person very well, don't you?

19
00:01:25,185 --> 00:01:29,756
Do you know this so-called Doctor X,
Professor Busujima?

20
00:01:30,390 --> 00:01:33,359
No. I only heard rumors.

21
00:01:34,494 --> 00:01:35,395
But you know,

22
00:01:36,196 --> 00:01:38,198
the more I hear about this doctor,

23
00:01:38,398 --> 00:01:41,434
the more I feel
there's a resemblance to someone.

24
00:01:43,703 --> 00:01:46,840
If such a skilled doctor actually exists,

25
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:50,009
I'd sure like to add
this person to my staff.

26
00:01:53,980 --> 00:01:54,981
That's right...

27
00:01:55,482 --> 00:01:57,617
I'll bring out some delicious melon.

28
00:01:59,185 --> 00:02:00,887
Thanks, but no thanks.

29
00:02:18,338 --> 00:02:20,707
GRACIAS
MICHIKO

30
00:02:45,365 --> 00:02:47,200
FREELANCE SURGEON
MICHIKO DAIMON

31
00:02:47,267 --> 00:02:50,970
48-year-old male needs emergency surgery
for peritonitis due to acute pancreatitis.

32
00:02:51,037 --> 00:02:54,440
I had to cancel my reservation
I finally made at that restaurant.

33
00:02:54,507 --> 00:02:55,508
I'm sorry.

34
00:02:56,276 --> 00:02:58,511
The freelancer's off on time again.
How nice.

35
00:02:58,578 --> 00:03:01,147
- Shall I take over the emergency surgery?
- No, thanks.

36
00:03:01,214 --> 00:03:03,650
Professor Torii was complaining
that your surgery costs too much.

37
00:03:03,716 --> 00:03:05,084
INSTRUCTOR
HIDEKI KAJI

38
00:03:05,151 --> 00:03:06,719
How much are you charging?

39
00:03:06,786 --> 00:03:07,620
I'm expensive...

40
00:03:07,687 --> 00:03:08,521
MAMORU HARA

41
00:03:08,588 --> 00:03:09,789
...since I don't make mistakes.

42
00:03:09,856 --> 00:03:12,425
- You're really infuriating!
- Dr. Kaji.

43
00:03:12,492 --> 00:03:16,763
They've already administered
anesthetics, so please hurry.

44
00:03:17,430 --> 00:03:20,200
Are you Dr. Daimon
from the Surgery Department? 

45
00:03:21,734 --> 00:03:24,737
The one who gets lots of money
for doing surgery?

46
00:03:25,638 --> 00:03:27,674
- So?
- My leg hurts. Operate on me.

47
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:28,942
INPATIENT
SAKI GOKITA

48
00:03:30,276 --> 00:03:31,844
Kids go to Pediatrics.

49
00:03:33,546 --> 00:03:36,583
- The doctor there is worthless.
- Worthless?

50
00:03:36,849 --> 00:03:39,752
I say it hurts, but he says
there's nothing wrong.

51
00:03:39,819 --> 00:03:42,021
If it hurts, there's something wrong.

52
00:03:42,722 --> 00:03:44,290
Can you fix it?

53
00:03:44,357 --> 00:03:48,027
Like I said, kids go to Pediatrics.
Besides, I don't like kids.

54
00:03:48,094 --> 00:03:50,496
- Dr. Daimon, please.
- Hey.

55
00:03:50,563 --> 00:03:54,300
- I'm not kidding, it really hurts.
- Cut it out. Give me a break.

56
00:03:55,668 --> 00:03:57,003
- Ouch.
- What?

57
00:03:58,938 --> 00:04:00,173
My leg hurts.

58
00:04:04,344 --> 00:04:07,547
- Dr. Daimon, what did you do?
- I didn't do anything.

59
00:04:07,614 --> 00:04:10,116
Did this scary doctor do something to you?

60
00:04:10,583 --> 00:04:12,352
My leg hurts.

61
00:04:12,418 --> 00:04:13,720
ASSISTANT
HIKARU MORIMOTO

62
00:04:17,490 --> 00:04:18,625
Ouch.

63
00:04:20,193 --> 00:04:21,060
What happened?

64
00:04:22,662 --> 00:04:26,366
- Saki, you again?
- Again?

65
00:04:26,833 --> 00:04:29,469
She was crying that her leg hurts,
so I brought her here.

66
00:04:29,936 --> 00:04:33,640
- If you'll excuse me, then.
- No. Dr. Daimon, please don't go.

67
00:04:35,241 --> 00:04:37,810
- It hurts.
- Don't worry about this child.

68
00:04:38,645 --> 00:04:40,246
Let's go back to your room.

69
00:04:40,313 --> 00:04:44,217
- No, my leg hurts.
- Okay. Shall we watch TV?

70
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:45,551
You'll be better if you watch TV.

71
00:04:45,618 --> 00:04:46,519
- Escort her back.
- Yes.

72
00:04:46,586 --> 00:04:49,789
Dr. Daimon, operate on me.
I'll pay you lots of money.

73
00:04:52,925 --> 00:04:55,928
PEDIATRIC SURGERY DEPARTMENT
TAKUYA KISHIDA

74
00:04:56,329 --> 00:04:57,964
So, you're Dr. Daimon.

75
00:04:58,464 --> 00:05:02,702
I've heard rumors about the new
brilliant doctor at Surgery Department 2.

76
00:05:03,169 --> 00:05:04,904
What's wrong with that child?

77
00:05:06,572 --> 00:05:08,541
Saki Gokita says that sometimes.

78
00:05:09,142 --> 00:05:10,977
Today, she said her leg hurts.

79
00:05:11,277 --> 00:05:14,781
- Yesterday, it was a stomachache.
- Is she faking an illness?

80
00:05:15,214 --> 00:05:17,684
It could be something psychological.

81
00:05:24,857 --> 00:05:28,227
- Is there something else?
- Why don't you examine her more?

82
00:05:28,928 --> 00:05:30,663
Did you do any tests? X-rays?

83
00:05:30,997 --> 00:05:32,732
All that was done, of course.

84
00:05:32,865 --> 00:05:34,634
Nothing abnormal showed up on X-ray.

85
00:05:35,902 --> 00:05:39,339
She was saying
that you're a worthless doctor.

86
00:05:42,942 --> 00:05:46,612
I'm her primary physician.
I know Saki better than anyone else.

87
00:05:46,679 --> 00:05:47,647
She's under good care.

88
00:05:48,781 --> 00:05:51,551
But of course.
Sorry for interfering. Excuse us.

89
00:06:03,363 --> 00:06:04,197
Thank you.

90
00:06:05,365 --> 00:06:06,199
Thank you!

91
00:06:06,265 --> 00:06:08,401
Tomorrow's discharge day.
Please take a picture with me!

92
00:06:08,468 --> 00:06:10,803
- Yes, of course.
- Would you, please?

93
00:06:11,003 --> 00:06:12,472
Say cheese!

94
00:06:13,373 --> 00:06:15,074
What the hell is that about?

95
00:06:15,141 --> 00:06:17,276
There's "wait out" for doctors, too.

96
00:06:17,643 --> 00:06:20,079
Dr. Kishida's the star
of the Pediatric Surgery Department.

97
00:06:20,146 --> 00:06:22,115
Thanks to him, there's been
an increase in patients.

98
00:06:22,181 --> 00:06:23,149
CHIEF NURSE
SONOKO CHIBA

99
00:06:23,216 --> 00:06:26,419
He's so nice to the children
and parents and explains patiently.

100
00:06:26,586 --> 00:06:28,788
He's a devoted
medical practitioner and researcher.

101
00:06:28,855 --> 00:06:30,490
He's found favor with the professor

102
00:06:30,556 --> 00:06:32,759
and became
an associate professor in his 30s.

103
00:06:32,825 --> 00:06:35,995
- He's popular with the nurses, too?
- As you can see, he's good-looking.

104
00:06:37,463 --> 00:06:39,732
It's not a contest for hosts.

105
00:06:39,899 --> 00:06:43,669
Those mothers who choose doctors
by their looks are empty-headed.

106
00:06:45,138 --> 00:06:46,372
There was a time...

107
00:06:46,439 --> 00:06:47,640
ANESTHESIOLOGIST
HIROMI JONOUCHI

108
00:06:47,707 --> 00:06:50,042
...I was temporarily empty-headed, too.

109
00:06:51,477 --> 00:06:52,645
What do you mean?

110
00:06:53,012 --> 00:06:54,914
Dr. Kishida divorced once and...

111
00:06:55,415 --> 00:06:57,617
he's Dr. Jonouchi's ex-husband.

112
00:06:57,717 --> 00:06:59,652
- What?
- Good night.

113
00:07:01,354 --> 00:07:03,456
Thank you as always. Thank you.

114
00:07:04,557 --> 00:07:08,161
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

115
00:07:09,028 --> 00:07:12,165
<i>University hospital medical offices</i>
<i>were losing power,</i>

116
00:07:12,265 --> 00:07:15,001
<i>and even medicine,</i>
<i>dealing with life and death,</i>

117
00:07:15,101 --> 00:07:17,737
<i>plunged into an era</i>
<i>where the law of the jungle prevailed.</i>

118
00:07:18,204 --> 00:07:19,605
Kishida, there you are.

119
00:07:19,672 --> 00:07:20,506
KEIICHIRO SOMA

120
00:07:21,607 --> 00:07:24,544
I'm sorry, Professor Soma. I was
getting ready for tomorrow's surgery.

121
00:07:41,561 --> 00:07:45,765
<i>To fill the critical shortage</i>
<i>in the medical field are the freelance.</i>

122
00:07:45,832 --> 00:07:48,835
<i>In other words, a lone wolf doctor.</i>

123
00:07:48,901 --> 00:07:51,370
The conference in Kanazawa
is right around the corner.

124
00:07:51,437 --> 00:07:52,572
Will you be ready?

125
00:07:52,638 --> 00:07:55,041
Professor, I'm sorry.
I'll get on it right away.

126
00:07:55,508 --> 00:07:57,343
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

127
00:07:57,844 --> 00:08:01,581
<i>She hates groups, she hates authority</i>
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

128
00:08:02,048 --> 00:08:06,252
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill to work her way up.</i>

129
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:08,454
- I'm back.
- Welcome back, Michiko.

130
00:08:09,155 --> 00:08:10,156
Look!

131
00:08:10,890 --> 00:08:14,193
Okay, I'll play one game with you.

132
00:08:14,393 --> 00:08:16,329
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

133
00:08:20,233 --> 00:08:21,534
<i>Also known as...</i>

134
00:08:22,401 --> 00:08:23,803
<i>Doctor X.</i>

135
00:08:30,710 --> 00:08:33,579
DOCTOR X SURGEON MICHIKO DAIMON
EPISODE 5

136
00:08:36,482 --> 00:08:39,685
The person taking lead
in Pediatric Surgery at the Third Hospital

137
00:08:39,752 --> 00:08:41,954
is Professor Soma
who's originally from the main hospital.

138
00:08:42,188 --> 00:08:43,422
- Soma?
- Yeah.

139
00:08:43,890 --> 00:08:46,826
He says satellite hospitals
are outposts of the main hospital,

140
00:08:46,893 --> 00:08:49,729
and uses the medical office
as his research tool.

141
00:08:49,795 --> 00:08:53,266
<i>He made Dr. Kishida an associate</i>
<i>because he was the most loyal.</i>

142
00:08:53,332 --> 00:08:56,102
Members of the medical staff
in the outpost have to find favor

143
00:08:56,369 --> 00:09:00,606
with the professors,
or else there's no future for them.

144
00:09:00,673 --> 00:09:02,375
Everyone's desperate
to get on their good side.

145
00:09:02,441 --> 00:09:03,276
AKIRA KANBARA

146
00:09:03,442 --> 00:09:07,113
I was like that back then, too.

147
00:09:07,179 --> 00:09:10,550
Didn't you get transferred
because you weren't good at brownnosing?

148
00:09:10,616 --> 00:09:13,219
You can't pay me enough
to go back there now.

149
00:09:13,286 --> 00:09:14,520
Yeah, I bet.

150
00:09:15,888 --> 00:09:17,890
Michiko, you don't even like kids.

151
00:09:17,957 --> 00:09:19,759
Why do you want to know
about Pediatric Surgery?

152
00:09:19,825 --> 00:09:22,795
A kid said she'd pay me
lots of money to operate on her.

153
00:09:22,862 --> 00:09:24,764
Wow, lots of money?

154
00:09:24,830 --> 00:09:27,400
But they won't let Surgery
handle Pediatrics.

155
00:09:27,466 --> 00:09:29,936
You'd better be careful
of that Professor Soma.

156
00:09:30,002 --> 00:09:32,104
He's like power in a doctor's gown.

157
00:09:33,406 --> 00:09:36,475
But all professors are like that.

158
00:09:36,542 --> 00:09:38,144
It's <i>ron.</i>

159
00:09:39,011 --> 00:09:40,580
<i>Chun, double dora.</i>

160
00:09:41,414 --> 00:09:45,084
- It's always like this.
- Thank you.

161
00:09:52,758 --> 00:09:54,126
Hello, this is Kishida.

162
00:09:57,129 --> 00:09:58,631
Please transfer the call.

163
00:10:01,734 --> 00:10:03,569
Hello. Is this Mai? What's up?

164
00:10:03,703 --> 00:10:08,641
Daddy, come to our Parents' Day
next Saturday.

165
00:10:10,509 --> 00:10:11,811
Next Saturday?

166
00:10:13,346 --> 00:10:16,949
I'd love to go, but I have to help
a very important professor.

167
00:10:17,750 --> 00:10:20,219
- Sorry.
- Daddy...

168
00:10:20,853 --> 00:10:22,355
Mom will be there, won't she?

169
00:10:23,723 --> 00:10:27,426
Mommy's busy with surgery,
so I don't know.

170
00:10:28,594 --> 00:10:29,562
<i>Oh, yeah?</i>

171
00:10:30,763 --> 00:10:33,766
<i>All right. I'll try to work something out.</i>

172
00:10:33,833 --> 00:10:37,336
- All right!
- It's getting late. Go to bed now.

173
00:10:46,779 --> 00:10:49,515
Dad's busy, so don't call him too often.

174
00:10:50,116 --> 00:10:53,886
- He'll come to Parents' Day!
- Really? That's great.

175
00:10:56,489 --> 00:11:01,127
TEITO MEDICAL UNIVERSITY THIRD HOSPITAL

176
00:11:05,998 --> 00:11:09,035
- What's the matter?
- Is Dr. Daimon here?

177
00:11:09,101 --> 00:11:11,804
Well, she's not here yet.

178
00:11:12,438 --> 00:11:14,173
I'll wait for her.

179
00:11:14,807 --> 00:11:17,576
- Saki, does it hurt again?
- My stomach.

180
00:11:17,910 --> 00:11:18,778
Ouch.

181
00:11:19,745 --> 00:11:22,314
- I'll go get a doctor from Pediatrics.
- Dr. Hara.

182
00:11:23,949 --> 00:11:27,219
They've run tests, but couldn't
find anything wrong with her.

183
00:11:28,421 --> 00:11:30,589
Children like
to make up illnesses, I guess.

184
00:11:35,061 --> 00:11:36,028
Saki.

185
00:11:36,929 --> 00:11:38,297
Here, you can have it. 

186
00:11:39,598 --> 00:11:41,067
You'll be cured with this.

187
00:11:41,734 --> 00:11:45,071
Don't think I'm stupid just because
I'm a kid. How can that cure me?

188
00:11:49,742 --> 00:11:51,343
- Shall I take over?
- Please.

189
00:11:54,747 --> 00:11:57,883
So, tell me,
what did you want with Dr. Daimon?

190
00:11:58,751 --> 00:12:00,820
It hurts, so I want her to do surgery.

191
00:12:00,886 --> 00:12:03,389
Surgery hurts even more,
so you shouldn't--

192
00:12:05,224 --> 00:12:06,392
I can have this?

193
00:12:07,727 --> 00:12:09,095
This is my favorite.

194
00:12:09,328 --> 00:12:12,231
Look, surgery is painful,
so you shouldn't get it.

195
00:12:12,298 --> 00:12:15,701
Especially Dr. Daimon.
You'd better stay away from her.

196
00:12:15,768 --> 00:12:18,304
Her true identity is
a devil in a doctor's gown.

197
00:12:18,370 --> 00:12:21,974
- Devil?
- Her real name is Michiko Demon--

198
00:12:22,041 --> 00:12:23,609
It's Michiko Daimon.

199
00:12:23,676 --> 00:12:25,911
I told you not to stand behind me.

200
00:12:27,747 --> 00:12:30,082
Dr. Daimon, my stomach hurts.

201
00:12:31,884 --> 00:12:32,818
Lie down.

202
00:12:37,723 --> 00:12:40,459
There's more than one part to a stomach.

203
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:43,095
- Speak more gently to kids.
- Ouch!

204
00:12:43,162 --> 00:12:45,397
- Is this where it hurts the most?
- Yes.

205
00:12:48,367 --> 00:12:50,503
Yesterday it was your leg,
and today it's your stomach?

206
00:12:50,569 --> 00:12:51,937
Do surgery on me and fix it.

207
00:12:52,004 --> 00:12:53,839
I can't without running some tests first.

208
00:12:53,906 --> 00:12:55,241
Then run some tests.

209
00:12:56,909 --> 00:13:00,312
Saki, let's go back to your room.
Everyone's worried and looking for you.

210
00:13:02,381 --> 00:13:05,518
- You're the anesthesia doctor, right?
- Yes. Let's go.

211
00:13:05,584 --> 00:13:08,020
The reason why it didn't hurt
when my stomach was cut,

212
00:13:08,087 --> 00:13:10,322
- was because I had anesthesia, right?
- Right.

213
00:13:10,389 --> 00:13:15,427
Doctor, give me anesthesia.
It really hurts. Please.

214
00:13:16,395 --> 00:13:18,430
That anesthesia is very strong,

215
00:13:18,497 --> 00:13:21,167
so we can only use it
for surgeries. Let's go.

216
00:13:23,702 --> 00:13:25,805
I wonder if Saki's really in pain.

217
00:13:25,871 --> 00:13:29,909
Hey. Stop butting into Pediatrics
trying to drum up business.

218
00:13:29,975 --> 00:13:31,310
No matter how you look at it,

219
00:13:31,410 --> 00:13:33,946
you're not the type
to be liked by children.

220
00:13:37,349 --> 00:13:41,453
So, she had surgery at this hospital.

221
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:46,926
Saki Gokita fell three months ago,

222
00:13:46,992 --> 00:13:49,962
and was brought in by an ambulance
with a hard blow to the abdomen.

223
00:13:50,029 --> 00:13:52,998
She was suffering from external wounds
as well as ruptured internal organs

224
00:13:53,098 --> 00:13:55,034
and an emergency surgery
was performed immediately.

225
00:13:55,134 --> 00:13:57,269
- Who performed the surgery?
- Professor Soma.

226
00:13:57,736 --> 00:13:58,804
The surgery was successful,

227
00:13:58,904 --> 00:14:01,440
prognosis was good and she was discharged,
but two months later,

228
00:14:01,507 --> 00:14:03,275
she came back having
a pain in her right knee.

229
00:14:03,342 --> 00:14:05,010
This is the X-ray from that time.

230
00:14:05,744 --> 00:14:06,745
There's nothing abnormal.

231
00:14:07,146 --> 00:14:10,716
Three days later, she had pain
in the right groin area and was retested.

232
00:14:10,850 --> 00:14:12,017
That image is here.

233
00:14:12,818 --> 00:14:13,919
There's nothing abnormal.

234
00:14:13,986 --> 00:14:15,120
And five days later,

235
00:14:15,221 --> 00:14:17,189
she was retested again
for pain in the mid-abdomen.

236
00:14:17,256 --> 00:14:18,224
That image is here.

237
00:14:19,225 --> 00:14:21,727
As you can see, there was
nothing abnormal in all three pictures.

238
00:14:22,294 --> 00:14:24,964
- Anything else? Any more pictures?
- There aren't any more.

239
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:26,465
They think the pain may be

240
00:14:26,532 --> 00:14:29,068
caused by stress
due to lack of maternal affection.

241
00:14:29,435 --> 00:14:31,537
Is that Professor Soma's diagnosis?

242
00:14:31,604 --> 00:14:32,438
Yes.

243
00:14:33,205 --> 00:14:35,107
But I'm impressed, Dr. Daimon,

244
00:14:35,407 --> 00:14:37,309
that you're even expanding
into Pediatrics.

245
00:14:37,977 --> 00:14:40,579
That child's parents are both CPAs.

246
00:14:40,646 --> 00:14:42,882
You must've picked up on
the fact that they're wealthy.

247
00:14:59,064 --> 00:15:00,132
Oh, it's you.

248
00:15:01,066 --> 00:15:01,901
What?

249
00:15:04,203 --> 00:15:08,474
It's about Saki.
Shouldn't you test her one more time?

250
00:15:08,540 --> 00:15:11,677
There's no need for that.
Professor Soma said so, too.

251
00:15:14,480 --> 00:15:17,116
"Professor said so, too."

252
00:15:19,385 --> 00:15:20,986
What are you trying to say?

253
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:27,726
There are times children lie
to get adults' attention.

254
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:29,328
As they keep on lying,

255
00:15:29,795 --> 00:15:31,997
they become unable to tell
what's fake and what's real,

256
00:15:32,064 --> 00:15:33,532
and they start hurting for real.

257
00:15:35,301 --> 00:15:36,869
There's a number of cases like that.

258
00:15:37,870 --> 00:15:39,171
She's just lonely.

259
00:15:41,507 --> 00:15:43,509
Her parents are busy all the time.

260
00:15:43,909 --> 00:15:47,446
The mother's love that should be devoted
to her child is directed towards work.

261
00:15:47,513 --> 00:15:48,981
It's pain born from loneliness

262
00:15:49,048 --> 00:15:50,916
of not being able
to be indulged by her parents.

263
00:15:52,384 --> 00:15:55,254
Hey. Why do you make
assumptions like that?

264
00:15:58,257 --> 00:15:59,858
That's how you always are.

265
00:15:59,992 --> 00:16:01,994
You were like that back then, too.

266
00:16:02,795 --> 00:16:04,997
Don't act like you can
see through children's feelings.

267
00:16:05,064 --> 00:16:06,465
Hey, calm down.

268
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:09,735
By the way,

269
00:16:10,302 --> 00:16:12,204
I got a call from Mai yesterday.

270
00:16:13,005 --> 00:16:15,307
Sounds like work's your priority
as usual, but like I said,

271
00:16:16,008 --> 00:16:18,777
if you're planning to continue
working as an anesthesiologist,

272
00:16:18,844 --> 00:16:20,813
my parents can take care of her.

273
00:16:21,981 --> 00:16:24,817
They're very concerned about Mai.

274
00:16:25,284 --> 00:16:28,754
- I'll raise Mai well on my own.
- Then why don't you...

275
00:16:29,922 --> 00:16:31,924
think about her a little bit more?

276
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:35,127
She needs her mother's love
the most at this age.

277
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:39,665
Anyway, you'll never take
Mai away from me.

278
00:16:41,066 --> 00:16:43,002
Actually...

279
00:16:43,802 --> 00:16:46,805
isn't it because the professor
messed up the surgery

280
00:16:46,872 --> 00:16:49,108
that Saki is in so much pain?

281
00:16:50,175 --> 00:16:51,710
Dr. Daimon, you were here?

282
00:16:52,177 --> 00:16:53,912
The surgery three months ago.

283
00:16:54,546 --> 00:16:57,082
Dr. Kishida, you attended
the surgery as the assistant, right?

284
00:16:58,283 --> 00:16:59,151
Yes.

285
00:16:59,218 --> 00:17:01,053
And Dr. Jonouchi was the anesthesiologist.

286
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:03,489
- That's right.
- So, how did it go?

287
00:17:03,722 --> 00:17:07,126
Did Professor Soma
make a mistake during surgery?

288
00:17:07,292 --> 00:17:10,429
That's an insult.
Professor Soma never makes mistakes.

289
00:17:11,430 --> 00:17:14,466
You, as the associate professor,
can't say anything against him.

290
00:17:15,567 --> 00:17:16,435
How was it?

291
00:17:17,536 --> 00:17:21,907
Well, it was a difficult surgery,
but there was no mistake.

292
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:23,742
It was a flawless surgery.

293
00:17:26,145 --> 00:17:27,212
I see.

294
00:17:29,515 --> 00:17:33,619
I'll disappear, so please carry on.

295
00:17:36,488 --> 00:17:38,023
Who does she think she is?

296
00:17:38,724 --> 00:17:40,392
She's a little different.

297
00:17:45,364 --> 00:17:46,198
Where were we?

298
00:17:47,366 --> 00:17:51,670
"Anyway, you'll never take
Mai away from me"...

299
00:17:54,873 --> 00:17:56,141
is where you stopped.

300
00:18:06,218 --> 00:18:07,553
How's your stomach?

301
00:18:08,187 --> 00:18:10,722
It hurt until a while ago,
but not anymore.

302
00:18:11,757 --> 00:18:12,724
I see.

303
00:18:13,859 --> 00:18:16,161
This is where it hurt yesterday, right?

304
00:18:16,228 --> 00:18:17,062
Right.

305
00:18:17,863 --> 00:18:19,231
And the day before yesterday?

306
00:18:19,765 --> 00:18:20,599
Here.

307
00:18:21,066 --> 00:18:26,338
Two days ago, here. Yesterday, here.
Until a while ago, here.

308
00:18:28,373 --> 00:18:30,876
- It moves around.
- That's right.

309
00:18:35,314 --> 00:18:36,982
How did you get that scar?

310
00:18:37,783 --> 00:18:39,551
Maybe from three months ago.

311
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:45,591
I heard you were brought here by ambulance
after you fell and blacked out.

312
00:18:45,724 --> 00:18:48,560
Yeah. By the time I woke up,
the surgery was over

313
00:18:48,694 --> 00:18:50,529
and I was in bed,
so I don't remember much.

314
00:18:50,662 --> 00:18:51,797
Where did you fall?

315
00:18:52,331 --> 00:18:56,168
When I went to the hot spring
with Grandma, I ran and slipped.

316
00:18:57,369 --> 00:18:59,404
Hot spring, huh?

317
00:18:59,471 --> 00:19:02,341
Why are you asking
when you won't operate on me?

318
00:19:02,474 --> 00:19:05,777
Because it's strange
that your pain moves around.

319
00:19:08,780 --> 00:19:12,017
If it starts hurting again,
send me a picture with this.

320
00:19:12,084 --> 00:19:13,018
Okay.

321
00:19:18,557 --> 00:19:19,825
Who the heck are you?

322
00:19:20,359 --> 00:19:21,460
What about you?

323
00:19:21,693 --> 00:19:23,829
This is Professor Soma,
Chief of Pediatrics Surgery.

324
00:19:25,264 --> 00:19:27,099
Why are you snooping around?

325
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:29,535
This is my Pediatric Surgery Department.

326
00:19:29,601 --> 00:19:32,504
My Pediatric Surgery Department? So what?

327
00:19:33,639 --> 00:19:34,506
Dr. Daimon.

328
00:19:35,674 --> 00:19:38,243
- Come with me.
- What for?

329
00:19:41,413 --> 00:19:43,615
A part-timer who isn't even
a member of the medical staff

330
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:46,451
looking up Pediatric Surgery's data
without permission

331
00:19:46,518 --> 00:19:48,353
is an unpardonable act of arrogance.

332
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:49,955
You're absolutely right.

333
00:19:50,122 --> 00:19:51,290
I apologize.

334
00:19:53,025 --> 00:19:54,993
Dr. Daimon, why did you do that?

335
00:19:55,060 --> 00:19:56,061
HOSPITAL DIRECTOR
RYUNOSUKE BUSUJIMA

336
00:19:57,262 --> 00:20:00,632
Saki Gokita. It's been three months
since she had surgery.

337
00:20:00,699 --> 00:20:02,401
It's not normal to have that kind of pain.

338
00:20:02,467 --> 00:20:04,736
Didn't I already explain that to you?

339
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:07,072
"There's nothing abnormal in test results.

340
00:20:07,139 --> 00:20:09,007
It's caused by lack
of maternal affection."

341
00:20:09,074 --> 00:20:12,211
That's what these doctors
keep repeating like a fool.

342
00:20:12,277 --> 00:20:13,278
Like a fool?

343
00:20:13,612 --> 00:20:14,746
CHIEF SURGEON
TAKASHI TORII

344
00:20:14,813 --> 00:20:17,516
She says it hurts.
There has to be a reason.

345
00:20:17,583 --> 00:20:19,885
A part-timer who knows nothing
about pediatric care.

346
00:20:19,985 --> 00:20:21,486
How dare you talk like you know it all!

347
00:20:21,787 --> 00:20:24,089
Dr. Torii, you must not be
educating her properly.

348
00:20:24,523 --> 00:20:27,326
With all due respect,
she isn't a part-timer, but freelancer.

349
00:20:27,392 --> 00:20:28,460
It's all the same.

350
00:20:29,094 --> 00:20:31,663
Besides, I'm not the one who hired her.

351
00:20:37,402 --> 00:20:40,205
And so? What's your diagnosis, Dr. Daimon?

352
00:20:43,408 --> 00:20:45,777
Pediatric Surgery Department Chief Soma,

353
00:20:45,911 --> 00:20:49,615
you made a mistake
during surgery, didn't you?

354
00:20:51,817 --> 00:20:52,651
What?

355
00:20:52,718 --> 00:20:54,519
You idiot! What an absurd thing to say.

356
00:20:54,987 --> 00:20:58,490
For the sake of Professor Soma's honor,
allow me to explain.

357
00:20:59,925 --> 00:21:01,927
When Saki Gokita was brought in,

358
00:21:01,994 --> 00:21:04,830
the liver was split in two and she was
in an extremely critical condition.

359
00:21:05,097 --> 00:21:08,166
The liver was crushed badly,
and hemostatic suturing was difficult.

360
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:11,136
Ordinarily, hepatectomy
would be performed.

361
00:21:11,336 --> 00:21:14,806
However, Professor Soma
used a freezer bag and temporarily

362
00:21:14,873 --> 00:21:16,775
closed the stomach
for a damage control surgery.

363
00:21:17,442 --> 00:21:20,045
The next day, he re-did the surgery
and sutured the liver.

364
00:21:20,445 --> 00:21:23,048
He successfully performed
an extremely difficult surgery.

365
00:21:23,415 --> 00:21:26,285
I believe his work will be praised
at this next convention as well.

366
00:21:27,185 --> 00:21:30,088
I'm calling it
Soma Damage Control Technique

367
00:21:30,155 --> 00:21:32,924
and I'm making
a presentation at the conference.

368
00:21:32,991 --> 00:21:34,226
Presentation? What?

369
00:21:34,293 --> 00:21:37,696
Is that right?
Very impressive, Professor Soma.

370
00:21:38,664 --> 00:21:40,065
I'm happy for you.

371
00:21:41,066 --> 00:21:42,401
Do you understand now?

372
00:21:44,403 --> 00:21:50,609
Please refrain from making
careless statements about medical errors.

373
00:21:52,311 --> 00:21:55,380
Do you understand? Dr. Daimon.

374
00:21:58,984 --> 00:22:00,452
This isn't good.

375
00:22:00,619 --> 00:22:02,988
I can't believe Demon wreaked havoc
at Pediatric Surgery, too.

376
00:22:03,055 --> 00:22:05,524
Our Professor Torii
and Professor Soma are fated rivals,

377
00:22:05,590 --> 00:22:07,726
battling it out
for the number of research papers.

378
00:22:07,793 --> 00:22:09,161
- Is that right?
- Yeah.

379
00:22:09,227 --> 00:22:11,897
They're the geeky type, and the kind
who loves papers and research,

380
00:22:11,963 --> 00:22:14,666
so that's why they're even more motivated
to win the promotion race.

381
00:22:14,733 --> 00:22:16,234
Who's winning?

382
00:22:16,301 --> 00:22:20,005
So far, they're dead even.
That's why Dr. Torii's frantic.

383
00:22:20,505 --> 00:22:21,440
I see.

384
00:22:23,041 --> 00:22:24,943
The very person who wreaked havoc is back.

385
00:22:34,419 --> 00:22:36,421
MY LEFT THIGH HURTS

386
00:22:56,308 --> 00:22:58,777
- What are you guys looking at?
- Nothing.

387
00:23:02,180 --> 00:23:03,281
I'm leaving.

388
00:23:14,025 --> 00:23:15,427
Ouch.

389
00:23:16,294 --> 00:23:17,462
Ouch.

390
00:23:17,996 --> 00:23:21,166
Ouch! Ouch...

391
00:23:27,005 --> 00:23:28,974
<i>Ron.</i> Four concealed triplets.

392
00:23:33,812 --> 00:23:35,313
Did she find a boyfriend?

393
00:23:36,248 --> 00:23:38,150
She's been waiting
for an e-mail all this time.

394
00:23:38,216 --> 00:23:41,853
There's no way Michiko would find a man.
Right, Ben Casey?

395
00:24:11,883 --> 00:24:12,884
Saki?

396
00:24:14,386 --> 00:24:15,520
Saki, are you okay?

397
00:24:18,457 --> 00:24:19,858
Does it still hurt?

398
00:24:27,532 --> 00:24:28,633
Ouch.

399
00:24:32,971 --> 00:24:34,739
Who are you e-mailing?

400
00:24:36,975 --> 00:24:38,343
Dr. Daimon.

401
00:24:39,911 --> 00:24:42,747
She told me to e-mail her
when it starts hurting.

402
00:25:06,538 --> 00:25:08,373
It's her leg today.

403
00:25:09,541 --> 00:25:11,176
It's moving again.

404
00:25:12,143 --> 00:25:13,645
Michiko.

405
00:25:14,446 --> 00:25:16,381
What?

406
00:25:16,615 --> 00:25:18,283
Doesn't the bath feel great?

407
00:25:19,851 --> 00:25:22,621
This is heaven.

408
00:25:24,289 --> 00:25:26,758
Big baths are wonderful, aren't they?

409
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:31,897
It improves your blood circulation
and rejuvenates you.

410
00:25:33,331 --> 00:25:34,966
Blood circulation?

411
00:25:37,636 --> 00:25:39,304
I'm getting out first.

412
00:25:39,704 --> 00:25:41,473
What! Are you getting out already?

413
00:25:41,540 --> 00:25:45,477
Hey, wait for me.
I'm getting out now, too. Wait!

414
00:26:27,252 --> 00:26:28,753
Ouch, ouch...

415
00:26:28,887 --> 00:26:33,892
I got out in a hurry,
so I slipped and fell and cut my hand.

416
00:26:33,959 --> 00:26:36,828
When we get home,
disinfect it and wrap a bandage, okay?

417
00:26:36,895 --> 00:26:38,163
Ouch. Ouch!

418
00:26:55,981 --> 00:26:58,216
The pain moves around.

419
00:27:00,785 --> 00:27:03,254
It's moving along the blood vessel.

420
00:27:06,591 --> 00:27:09,594
- I want you to test Saki again.
- That's impossible.

421
00:27:09,728 --> 00:27:12,731
Professor Soma's being sensitive
after being accused

422
00:27:12,797 --> 00:27:14,733
of making a medical error
in front of the Director.

423
00:27:14,799 --> 00:27:18,203
What's more important, humoring
the professor or your patient's life?

424
00:27:19,571 --> 00:27:20,705
You're exaggerating.

425
00:27:21,239 --> 00:27:23,475
I told you her pain is psychological--

426
00:27:23,541 --> 00:27:26,478
- She's not lying about it.
- Calm down.

427
00:27:27,178 --> 00:27:30,782
You've lost your composure
as a doctor to make sound judgment.

428
00:27:30,849 --> 00:27:31,683
That's you.

429
00:27:31,750 --> 00:27:34,886
See, there you go,
bringing personal feelings into it.

430
00:27:40,358 --> 00:27:42,160
Why won't you examine her
when she's hurting?

431
00:27:43,828 --> 00:27:45,463
Just one more time.

432
00:27:46,531 --> 00:27:47,532
Please.

433
00:27:49,668 --> 00:27:52,470
- Kishida, is the car ready?
- Yes.

434
00:27:54,973 --> 00:27:55,940
Wait.

435
00:27:56,574 --> 00:27:59,544
We're on our way to Kanazawa
for the Pediatric Surgery Conference.

436
00:28:15,193 --> 00:28:18,329
Michiko, please. It hurts.

437
00:28:19,364 --> 00:28:20,231
What?

438
00:28:21,366 --> 00:28:24,235
- How did you get this?
- I got it at the bath.

439
00:28:24,302 --> 00:28:25,370
At the bath?

440
00:28:25,437 --> 00:28:28,339
I slipped and fell
and got pricked by a fragment.

441
00:28:30,041 --> 00:28:32,744
- Ouch, ouch!
- What did you get pricked by?

442
00:28:32,811 --> 00:28:35,246
I told you, a piece of tile.

443
00:28:37,882 --> 00:28:39,751
How did you get that scar?
Where did you fall?

444
00:28:39,818 --> 00:28:42,654
When I went to the hot spring
with Grandma,

445
00:28:43,021 --> 00:28:44,389
I ran and slipped.

446
00:28:45,523 --> 00:28:48,259
A bath. A piece of tile...

447
00:28:48,326 --> 00:28:50,562
Hey, will you hurry up? It hurts.

448
00:28:50,628 --> 00:28:54,299
A fragment got entrapped
in the blood vessel, and that moved,

449
00:28:55,467 --> 00:28:58,069
impeding blood flow
and causing inflammation.

450
00:28:58,737 --> 00:29:00,872
- No wonder it hurts.
- What?

451
00:29:00,939 --> 00:29:02,974
Which means next is...

452
00:29:18,923 --> 00:29:20,625
IT HURTS UNDER MY CHEST

453
00:29:26,998 --> 00:29:29,134
If we don't take it out right away,
her life's in danger.

454
00:29:29,934 --> 00:29:35,106
Ouch. Ouch!

455
00:29:44,015 --> 00:29:45,650
I'LL BE THERE SOON

456
00:29:53,324 --> 00:29:55,894
"It hurts, it hurts.

457
00:29:56,394 --> 00:30:02,867
The sea water stings my body.
I was deceived by the gods.

458
00:30:02,967 --> 00:30:05,203
It hurts so much, I feel like I'm dying."

459
00:30:06,504 --> 00:30:07,639
Mommy.

460
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:10,809
Daddy will come, won't he?

461
00:30:11,543 --> 00:30:12,510
To Parents' Day?

462
00:30:13,678 --> 00:30:17,348
I'm not sure about Dad.
He had to go far away for a conference.

463
00:30:17,882 --> 00:30:22,487
What? But he promised me.
Daddy doesn't lie.

464
00:30:31,763 --> 00:30:33,765
- Yes, hello?
<i>- This is Daimon.</i>

465
00:30:34,165 --> 00:30:36,234
<i>- Please come to the hospital immediately.</i>
- What?

466
00:30:36,301 --> 00:30:38,703
Saki's telling me
she has a pain in her chest.

467
00:30:38,970 --> 00:30:40,905
The pain moving in such a short time means

468
00:30:40,972 --> 00:30:43,074
foreign material is entrapped
in the blood vessel.

469
00:30:43,274 --> 00:30:46,344
It may move into the heart
if we don't operate now.

470
00:30:46,845 --> 00:30:49,347
We're performing an emergency surgery.
Please come right away.

471
00:30:50,615 --> 00:30:52,050
I can't, it's too late.

472
00:30:52,116 --> 00:30:53,384
Please!

473
00:31:02,894 --> 00:31:04,529
Please call Morimoto immediately.

474
00:31:04,729 --> 00:31:06,331
He's not on duty today, so he isn't here.

475
00:31:06,397 --> 00:31:07,665
Then, Dr. Hara, you'll do.

476
00:31:07,732 --> 00:31:09,901
What do you mean I'll do? What's going on?

477
00:31:09,968 --> 00:31:12,403
First, X-ray examination
under general anesthesia.

478
00:31:12,470 --> 00:31:14,105
- Yes.
- Which OR is available?

479
00:31:14,172 --> 00:31:15,640
Wait, you didn't get an approval?

480
00:31:15,707 --> 00:31:17,742
At this time, they're all available.

481
00:31:20,511 --> 00:31:21,746
Dr. Daimon.

482
00:31:22,780 --> 00:31:23,715
Don't worry.

483
00:31:24,182 --> 00:31:25,750
I don't make mistakes.

484
00:31:35,260 --> 00:31:39,697
KANAZAWA

485
00:31:50,141 --> 00:31:52,510
We're celebrating
the successful convention today.

486
00:31:52,577 --> 00:31:55,546
- You drink, too.
- Yes, thank you.

487
00:31:56,748 --> 00:31:59,284
You're finally in the driver's seat
to become the next director.

488
00:32:00,018 --> 00:32:01,286
Congratulations.

489
00:32:03,254 --> 00:32:04,155
Kishida.

490
00:32:04,889 --> 00:32:07,125
No one else can take over your duties.

491
00:32:07,392 --> 00:32:08,927
I'm counting on you from now on, too.

492
00:32:09,961 --> 00:32:10,795
Yes.

493
00:32:15,733 --> 00:32:16,701
Excuse me.

494
00:32:19,070 --> 00:32:20,004
Hello.

495
00:32:21,806 --> 00:32:23,708
What? Emergency surgery?

496
00:32:24,375 --> 00:32:26,811
- Our patient, Saki Gokita?
- What was that?

497
00:32:26,878 --> 00:32:29,847
Yes. Dr. Daimon said
there wasn't a moment to spare

498
00:32:29,914 --> 00:32:32,417
and went into the operating room just now.

499
00:32:33,251 --> 00:32:35,320
Stop her! I will not allow such a thing.

500
00:32:57,175 --> 00:32:58,443
Dr. Daimon.

501
00:32:58,910 --> 00:33:00,979
After administering
general anesthesia to a child,

502
00:33:01,079 --> 00:33:02,780
what are you going to do
if you misdiagnose?

503
00:33:03,715 --> 00:33:05,249
We got her family's consent at least.

504
00:33:11,656 --> 00:33:13,024
Nothing's coming into the picture.

505
00:33:13,858 --> 00:33:17,395
We already tested a number of times.
You saw it, too, Dr. Daimon.

506
00:33:17,662 --> 00:33:19,530
Nothing abnormal was detected.

507
00:33:20,665 --> 00:33:22,767
Doing such a thing
in Professor Soma's absence,

508
00:33:23,334 --> 00:33:25,603
- you won't get away with it.
- Stop grumbling.

509
00:33:43,254 --> 00:33:44,288
Found it.

510
00:33:47,759 --> 00:33:48,860
Foreign material found.

511
00:33:50,061 --> 00:33:51,362
What could it be?

512
00:33:51,662 --> 00:33:53,131
It looks like a thin needle.

513
00:33:53,197 --> 00:33:56,467
Don't tell me it got entrapped
during the professor's surgery.

514
00:33:56,534 --> 00:33:58,636
What? A medical error?

515
00:34:03,074 --> 00:34:03,908
No.

516
00:34:04,342 --> 00:34:07,779
- It's probably a piece of tile.
- A tile?

517
00:34:09,247 --> 00:34:10,681
See this scar here?

518
00:34:11,883 --> 00:34:15,787
When she fell at the hot spring,
a broken piece entered through this wound.

519
00:34:15,853 --> 00:34:17,021
Vitals?

520
00:34:17,088 --> 00:34:20,158
Blood pressure 90 over 55.
Heart rate 110 and rising.

521
00:34:20,658 --> 00:34:22,627
Possibly a burden on the venous system.

522
00:34:23,428 --> 00:34:26,464
We'll open the abdomen and remove
the foreign material in the blood vessel.

523
00:34:28,399 --> 00:34:30,001
Please take away the C-arm.

524
00:34:30,835 --> 00:34:31,769
Excuse me.

525
00:34:37,108 --> 00:34:38,042
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

526
00:34:57,795 --> 00:34:58,663
This must be it.

527
00:34:59,163 --> 00:35:01,165
Blood flow is obstructed
in the hepatic vein.

528
00:35:01,232 --> 00:35:03,034
Put clamps above
and below the foreign material

529
00:35:03,101 --> 00:35:04,569
and cut off blood flow.

530
00:35:04,635 --> 00:35:05,770
- Satinsky.
- Yes.

531
00:35:06,637 --> 00:35:08,706
Please declamp within 15 minutes.

532
00:35:09,173 --> 00:35:10,441
- The other one.
- Yes.

533
00:35:14,545 --> 00:35:15,513
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

534
00:35:27,592 --> 00:35:28,526
Hello.

535
00:35:29,694 --> 00:35:31,462
Professor Soma. This is Torii.

536
00:35:33,664 --> 00:35:36,334
I'm not sure what
the emergency surgery's for.

537
00:35:36,434 --> 00:35:37,802
I just got here, too.

538
00:35:37,869 --> 00:35:40,304
How can you be so nonchalant about it?

539
00:35:41,139 --> 00:35:44,542
A freelance surgeon performing
unauthorized surgery on our patient

540
00:35:44,609 --> 00:35:45,877
is an unprecedented scandal!

541
00:35:49,780 --> 00:35:51,215
- Forceps.
- Yes.

542
00:35:52,650 --> 00:35:54,785
- Rinse with saline.
- Got it.

543
00:36:10,568 --> 00:36:12,870
To think that was moving
in the blood vessel...

544
00:36:13,538 --> 00:36:15,306
the pain must've been excruciating.

545
00:36:21,445 --> 00:36:23,447
Twelve more minutes. Please hurry.

546
00:36:24,849 --> 00:36:27,018
- It's already sutured.
- What?

547
00:36:31,822 --> 00:36:32,790
What's the time?

548
00:36:32,857 --> 00:36:35,226
Three minutes, 15 seconds
from the time the clamps went on.

549
00:36:35,293 --> 00:36:36,460
Three minutes?

550
00:36:38,529 --> 00:36:40,698
- Resuming blood flow.
- Yes.

551
00:36:48,506 --> 00:36:50,007
I'm glad we found it.

552
00:36:52,410 --> 00:36:54,212
- Finish.
- Yes.

553
00:36:54,579 --> 00:36:57,715
- We're closing up.
- Tell me exactly what happened.

554
00:36:58,749 --> 00:37:03,287
Surgery Department 2 picked up
what Pediatric Surgery overlooked.

555
00:37:03,921 --> 00:37:04,755
Don't worry.

556
00:37:05,389 --> 00:37:06,958
Surgery Department 2 is outstanding.

557
00:37:39,757 --> 00:37:43,094
Saki, you were a warrior.

558
00:37:44,495 --> 00:37:50,167
One, two, three, four, five.

559
00:37:50,968 --> 00:37:54,372
Mr. White Rabbit,
there's more of us, isn't there?

560
00:37:54,438 --> 00:37:57,942
You're a fool, Mr. Shark.
You guys were deceived.

561
00:37:58,009 --> 00:38:02,980
Deceived? White Rabbit, you!

562
00:38:04,548 --> 00:38:07,385
Come here, I'm going to eat you.

563
00:38:07,985 --> 00:38:10,054
Wait.

564
00:38:12,089 --> 00:38:15,126
Mai, why don't we take a break?

565
00:38:15,493 --> 00:38:18,529
No! I have to show this
to Daddy on Parents' Day.

566
00:38:19,397 --> 00:38:21,766
- Yes.
- One more time.

567
00:38:21,832 --> 00:38:24,635
What? Okay.

568
00:38:25,469 --> 00:38:30,574
White Rabbit, you! I'm going to eat you.

569
00:38:32,843 --> 00:38:35,279
Sorry to keep you waiting, Mai. I'm home.

570
00:38:35,346 --> 00:38:37,048
Mommy.

571
00:38:37,348 --> 00:38:40,885
Thank you for taking care of her.
Here, say thank you to him.

572
00:38:40,951 --> 00:38:45,056
- Thank you, Mr. Shark.
- You're very welcome, White Rabbit.

573
00:38:46,490 --> 00:38:47,658
Thank you.

574
00:38:48,359 --> 00:38:50,094
Mr. Shark.

575
00:38:51,362 --> 00:38:52,296
Good job.

576
00:38:53,431 --> 00:38:54,265
Let's go home.

577
00:38:58,002 --> 00:39:02,473
<i>Professor Busujima</i>
<i>will now make his rounds.</i>

578
00:39:11,248 --> 00:39:15,252
Sir, my presentation was the hot topic
at the conference in Kanazawa.

579
00:39:23,260 --> 00:39:27,198
What's he planning to do?
He didn't even make eye contact.

580
00:39:28,966 --> 00:39:33,804
Don't tell me Busujima's
planning to cast me aside.

581
00:39:37,608 --> 00:39:39,143
Dr. Daimon.

582
00:39:40,177 --> 00:39:43,047
Michiko, you should've found it sooner
and done a quick surgery!

583
00:39:43,447 --> 00:39:46,717
It didn't show on X-ray,
so I couldn't help it.

584
00:39:46,784 --> 00:39:48,386
You took too much time.

585
00:39:51,021 --> 00:39:55,659
But, Saki,
after she found the tile fragment,

586
00:39:56,093 --> 00:39:58,929
it only took three minutes
for her to remove it.

587
00:39:59,463 --> 00:40:00,431
Three minutes?

588
00:40:01,031 --> 00:40:02,700
I see... I'm seeing you in a new light.

589
00:40:03,801 --> 00:40:06,036
- Hey!
- It doesn't hurt anymore?

590
00:40:06,103 --> 00:40:10,541
Yep. Michiko and Dr. Hiromi,
you're the only ones who believed me.

591
00:40:28,259 --> 00:40:30,394
Okay, let's put on your bunny ears.

592
00:40:30,461 --> 00:40:33,230
Mai, this is cute.
It really looks good on you.

593
00:40:35,199 --> 00:40:36,434
Daddy's here!

594
00:40:39,403 --> 00:40:40,938
- Mai!
- Daddy!

595
00:40:41,172 --> 00:40:43,174
I bet you're happy, Mom made it, too.

596
00:40:43,240 --> 00:40:46,043
I'm surprised you got a day off.
What about the professor's research?

597
00:40:46,744 --> 00:40:47,978
I skipped it.

598
00:40:48,813 --> 00:40:53,017
Daddy, pay attention and watch
"The White Rabbit of Inaba," okay?

599
00:40:53,083 --> 00:40:55,920
I sure will. Oh, you have to go get ready.

600
00:40:56,187 --> 00:40:57,922
Mai, let's get back in there.

601
00:41:00,324 --> 00:41:01,892
Are you sure you're okay?

602
00:41:03,761 --> 00:41:05,329
This is more important.

603
00:41:10,201 --> 00:41:12,002
Saki wasn't lying.

604
00:41:13,204 --> 00:41:15,406
My sense of guilt for not making time

605
00:41:16,140 --> 00:41:19,210
to see Mai could be why
I made the wrong diagnosis.

606
00:41:21,178 --> 00:41:22,246
That's what I thought.

607
00:41:25,015 --> 00:41:26,851
Here I am, a pediatric surgeon,

608
00:41:27,318 --> 00:41:29,820
and I didn't understand
a child's feelings.

609
00:41:31,856 --> 00:41:32,823
You're too soft.

610
00:41:33,290 --> 00:41:35,493
You're going to miss your chance
to be a professor.

611
00:41:38,229 --> 00:41:40,998
Okay, everyone.
We're moving to the other room.

612
00:41:41,065 --> 00:41:43,868
- Okay!
- Come along!

613
00:41:44,768 --> 00:41:45,970
Hurry, hurry!

614
00:41:47,204 --> 00:41:48,305
Good luck.

615
00:41:52,710 --> 00:41:53,677
Come in.

616
00:41:56,413 --> 00:41:57,948
I'm here again.

617
00:41:59,116 --> 00:42:02,686
I've brought you a melon
for the emergency surgery the other day.

618
00:42:08,259 --> 00:42:11,095
Here's the bill for that.

619
00:42:13,264 --> 00:42:14,465
So much again.

620
00:42:14,532 --> 00:42:15,399
630,000 YEN

621
00:42:17,968 --> 00:42:20,504
By the way, what's this babysitting fee?

622
00:42:31,549 --> 00:42:35,653
About that Doctor X
you were talking about the other day.

623
00:42:36,820 --> 00:42:38,589
If there's an X,

624
00:42:39,323 --> 00:42:44,161
does it mean Doctor Y
and Doctor Z also exist?

625
00:42:46,797 --> 00:42:48,899
Are you saying you don't know?

626
00:42:50,968 --> 00:42:52,803
Let's change the subject, then.

627
00:42:57,141 --> 00:42:58,509
Ten years ago.

628
00:43:01,345 --> 00:43:04,715
The one who shut down
Michiko Daimon's father's clinic.

629
00:43:08,419 --> 00:43:10,054
It wasn't me.

630
00:43:21,432 --> 00:43:22,833
<i>She hates groups,</i>

631
00:43:23,667 --> 00:43:27,037
<i>she hates authority,</i>
<i>and she hates restraints.</i>

632
00:43:29,740 --> 00:43:33,811
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill to work her way up.</i>

633
00:43:49,426 --> 00:43:51,829
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

634
00:43:57,234 --> 00:43:58,268
<i>Also known as...</i>

635
00:43:58,335 --> 00:43:59,336
CLINIC

636
00:43:59,670 --> 00:44:01,338
<i>...Doctor X.</i>

637
00:45:27,991 --> 00:45:29,126
This drama is fiction. All names of people
and organizations are fictional.

638
00:45:29,193 --> 00:45:30,294
Medical practices in the drama vary
depending on a person's medical condition.

639
00:45:30,360 --> 00:45:31,361
Subtitle translation by Kelly True

640
00:45:31,428 --> 00:45:32,262
PREVIEW

641
00:45:32,329 --> 00:45:33,731
He'll die if we leave him.

642
00:45:33,797 --> 00:45:35,699
<i>He has no talent whatsoever.</i>

643
00:45:35,766 --> 00:45:37,101
<i>Don't tell anyone.</i>

644
00:45:37,167 --> 00:45:39,670
- You have hilar bile duct cancer.
- That's enough!

645
00:45:39,737 --> 00:45:41,138
Are you trying to deceive me?

646
00:45:41,205 --> 00:45:42,473
I'll cut him open and save him.

647
00:45:42,539 --> 00:45:44,241
- He'll die if you do that.
<i>- Come now!</i>

648
00:45:44,308 --> 00:45:46,176
<i>- Emergency surgery.</i>
<i>- He's crashed.</i>
